DECISIONS
- The evidence item's amount is the GROSS rent the statement evidences, not the
  amount disbursed, so the manifest agrees with the income line it supports.
- A SECOND percentage calculation in financial-position-view (the monthly
  cash-flow projection, ~line 505) was deliberately LEFT on the percentage
  model, with a comment explaining why: it is forward-looking, so a percentage
  of projected rent is the correct basis, and resolveAgentFees is
  financial-year scoped with no meaning for a single month. Without that comment
  the next reader would "fix" it and break the projection.
- The useMemo dependency array gained rentalPaymentsByPropertyId,
  financialYearEnd, financialYearStartMonth and financialYearStartDay. Omitting
  them would have left the view showing stale fees after a statement was
  confirmed — a silent wrong number, which is the failure mode this whole track
  is about.

