A SPEC CONFLICT FOUND, NOT YET RESOLVED — acceptance criterion 5
Criterion 5 says the blinds should appear "classified as capital/Div 40". That
is NOT achievable in the current model. The expense classification vocabulary is
Repair | Capital Works | Immediate Repair (lib/tax/classification.ts); Division
40 reaches the schedule only via depreciation_reports.div40_annual, a quantity
surveyor's figure, and there is no way to mark an individual expense as a Div 40
depreciating asset. The $2,146 blinds expense is currently classified "Repair",
so the whole amount is deducted in FY2026.

Criterion 5's real purpose — that the blinds appear exactly ONCE and are not
double-counted via other_outgoings — is achievable and is what should be
asserted. The Division 40 half was over-specified from the tax treatment without
checking the model supported it. To be raised with the user before the phase
closes.
